# CODEOWNERS — terraform-provider-laravel-cloud
#
# GitHub uses this file to auto-request reviews from the listed owners
# whenever a matching path is touched. Every unmatched path falls
# through to the global `*` line at the bottom.
#
# Order matters — the LAST matching pattern wins. So specialised
# patterns for hot paths (release scripts, .github/) live below the
# broad-brush `*` fallback so specialists get the review.
#
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Everything defaults to the workspace maintainer.
*                                    @akouta

# The API-client + provider hotpaths — same owner for now; keeping the
# pattern here documents where a future co-maintainer would slot in.
/internal/api/                       @akouta
/internal/provider/                  @akouta

# Release + CI touch-points — every mutation gates on a full
# GoReleaser dry-run.
/.github/                            @akouta
/.goreleaser.yml                     @akouta
/GNUmakefile                         @akouta

# Docs live alongside code but are safe to auto-approve for the same
# owner. Kept as a distinct block so a future tech-writer role has an
# obvious slot.
/docs/                               @akouta
/examples/                           @akouta
